{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/318040-making-an-abyssal-for-the-first-time","id":318040,"title":"Making an Abyssal for the First Time","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Abyssal Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-11-21T00:46:46-08:00","id":318040,"title":"Making an Abyssal for the First Time","content":"I think I have have my rogue Abyssal figured out pretty well, but I noticed that the mirrored charm trees aren't a perfect match, like I was surprised Iron Kettle Body didn't have a mirror charm despite the fact it's an upgrade for Durability of Oak which does have one. I'm guessing there is some sort of overall balance with the charms that makes up for this?<br /> <br /> Also what is your experience using the alternate rules for resonance from Shards? To me they seem much more playable and far less punitive for characters who don't just want to be straight up murder machines.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1522-turkeygiant","name":"turkeygiant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1522_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"999"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-21T00:51:54-08:00","id":318064,"title":"","content":"I don't like that the alternate rules essentially gives Abyssals Solar Limit Breaks. Part of their appeal is that they DON'T have the Great Curse!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-21T02:27:05-08:00","id":318108,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/318040-making-an-abyssal-for-the-first-time?p=318064#post318064\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't like that the alternate rules essentially gives Abyssals Solar Limit Breaks. Part of their appeal is that they DON'T have the Great Curse!</div> </div> </div> </div>I found the distinction fairly academic in Second Edition when a 10 point Resonance eruption can come with being outright possessed by the Neverborn.<br /> But then I've seen Doom of the Black Sun in action and found it Curse of the Mother Hen levels of hilarious.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-21T06:11:04-08:00","id":318189,"title":"","content":"I have made <a href=\"http://boneandebony.livejournal.com/tag/abyssal\" target=\"_blank\">about 50 custom Abyssal Charms</a> in case you find that you miss an effect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.redbubble.com/people/nesling/works/15673780-loch-ness-monster-on-vacation?c=409846-mixed&amp;p=throw-pillow\" target=\"_blank\">Loch Ness monsters. On vacation. On a pillow.</a><br /> <br /> <br /> My wife is on <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/1Ngo336SKXWmoRnG3QWmhS\" target=\"_blank\">Spotify</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/864-jutlander","name":"Jutlander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"467"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-21T07:37:50-08:00","id":318236,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>turkeygiant</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/318040-making-an-abyssal-for-the-first-time#post318040\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think I have have my rogue Abyssal figured out pretty well, but I noticed that the mirrored charm trees aren't a perfect match, like I was surprised Iron Kettle Body didn't have a mirror charm despite the fact it's an upgrade for Durability of Oak which does have one. I'm guessing there is some sort of overall balance with the charms that makes up for this?</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't look for any real rhyme or reason there. If you want to port IKB, there's no real reason not to just invent a hombrew Resistance Charm to fill the hole left in the canon charmset.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-21T08:34:18-08:00","id":318270,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>turkeygiant</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/318040-making-an-abyssal-for-the-first-time#post318040\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think I have have my rogue Abyssal figured out pretty well, but I noticed that the mirrored charm trees aren't a perfect match, like I was surprised Iron Kettle Body didn't have a mirror charm despite the fact it's an upgrade for Durability of Oak which does have one. I'm guessing there is some sort of overall balance with the charms that makes up for this?<br /> <br /> Also what is your experience using the alternate rules for resonance from Shards? To me they seem much more playable and far less punitive for characters who don't just want to be straight up murder machines.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Iron Kettle did get a mirror in the errata. It is called Resilient Corpse Body.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2132-ejtaka","name":"Ejtaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2132_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1064"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-21T11:53:18-08:00","id":318402,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ejtaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/318040-making-an-abyssal-for-the-first-time?p=318270#post318270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Iron Kettle did get a mirror in the errata. It is called Resilient Corpse Body.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Are you sure your not thinking of Ox-body which is suggested to be called Corpse Body Resilience in the Abyssals Manual? I don't see errata for Iron Kettle Body...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1522-turkeygiant","name":"turkeygiant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1522_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"999"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-21T11:59:09-08:00","id":318404,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/318040-making-an-abyssal-for-the-first-time?p=318064#post318064\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't like that the alternate rules essentially gives Abyssals Solar Limit Breaks. Part of their appeal is that they DON'T have the Great Curse!</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm going to be playing in a mixed game and as free Abyssal, the last incarnation of the exaltation killed their Deathlord in a nihilistic suicide run, so I think the track less focused on servitude is better.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1522-turkeygiant","name":"turkeygiant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1522_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"999"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-21T12:08:27-08:00","id":318408,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/318040-making-an-abyssal-for-the-first-time?p=318064#post318064\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't like that the alternate rules essentially gives Abyssals Solar Limit Breaks. Part of their appeal is that they DON'T have the Great Curse!</div> </div> </div> </div>There's nothing appealing about Resonance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-21T12:28:22-08:00","id":318416,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/318040-making-an-abyssal-for-the-first-time?p=318408#post318408\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's nothing appealing about Resonance.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's your opinion, not an objective fact.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-21T14:12:15-08:00","id":318498,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>turkeygiant</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/318040-making-an-abyssal-for-the-first-time?p=318402#post318402\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Are you sure your not thinking of Ox-body which is suggested to be called Corpse Body Resilience in the Abyssals Manual? I don't see errata for Iron Kettle Body...</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Nope. Abyssals get Ox-Body Technique, just like everyone else.<br /> <br /> I spent some time digging it up. It's in Glories of the Most High: The Unconquered Sun P.27. It's really buried. Look for the Charm Armored in Righteousness Stance. Then look at the Abyssal Mirror for that called Flesh as Marble Stance. Then look for its prerequisite Charm Resilient Corpse Body, which is named there as being identical to Iron Kettle.<br /> <br /> And people wonder why I hate the Mirror keyword. There damn Charms are scattered everywhere, and you can't find them by skimming. It's not called out anywhere, just buried inside a different Charm, and referenced that it exists.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2132,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2132-ejtaka","user":"Ejtaka","date":".  Edited to insert page number into book reference. 11-21-2014, 05:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2132-ejtaka","name":"Ejtaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2132_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1064"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-21T16:01:00-08:00","id":318551,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ejtaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/318040-making-an-abyssal-for-the-first-time?p=318498#post318498\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Nope. Abyssals get Ox-Body Technique, just like everyone else.<br /> <br /> I spent some time digging it up. It's in Glories of the Most High: The Unconquered Sun P.27. It's really buried. Look for the Charm Armored in Righteousness Stance. Then look at the Abyssal Mirror for that called Flesh as Marble Stance. Then look for its prerequisite Charm Resilient Corpse Body, which is named there as being identical to Iron Kettle.<br /> <br /> And people wonder why I hate the Mirror keyword. There damn Charms are scattered everywhere, and you can't find them by skimming. It's not called out anywhere, just buried inside a different Charm, and referenced that it exists.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Man it doesn't help when they name two charms the same thing, Abyssals do get Ox-Body, you're right, but in the fluff of the charm they suggest that Abyssals would call it Corpse Body Resilience...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1522-turkeygiant","name":"turkeygiant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1522_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"999"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-21T16:07:21-08:00","id":318555,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/318040-making-an-abyssal-for-the-first-time?p=318064#post318064\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't like that the alternate rules essentially gives Abyssals Solar Limit Breaks. Part of their appeal is that they DON'T have the Great Curse!</div> </div> </div> </div>And the alternative to that is the standard Resonance rules.<br /> <br /> Which do such things as;<br /> <br /> A) Tearing open a Shadowland, blighting a large area outside of said Shadowland, possibly killing nearby mortals, and alerting Heaven to your presence.<br /> B) Shoot any attempts at social interactions not based on intimidation squarely in the nuts for at least a day.<br /> C) Removes an Intimacy that the Neverborn don't like, so basically anything that doesn't align with their goal of killing everything, or else twist it around into hate, no save, or else putting a 1 Willpower tax on any actions they don't like, or can control you if you don't spend will power to resist them, followed by the Neverborn possessing you to do as they see fit.<br /> D) renders all mote expenditure Peripheral, inflicting a number of unsoakable lethal levels of damage that may or may not drop you to Incapacitated or else inflict a random Crippling effect on you.<br /> <br /> So yeah. I'mma go with the Solar Limit Breaks. Much easier to deal with than having to worry about a dead cthonic horror ramming their clammy hand firmly up my character's ass and using them as a puppet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://s3.amazonaws.com/ksr/avatars/3507685/Exalted_Back.small.jpg?1370109312\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <hr />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/446-nervaqus987","name":"Nervaqus987","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar446_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-21T18:15:34-08:00","id":318602,"title":"","content":"The other thing I just ran into is figuring out how to respire essence. I'm playing a mortal who is going to pick up an unbound Abyssal Exaltation (No Deathlord or Monstrance) so I can't rely on going back to a shadowland every night, and vampire murder-hobo sprees can be hard to explain to the party. From what I understand a hearthstone is the solution, so I picked one up. It seems like the Abyssal respiration rules are really punitive in a basically un-fun way, were they maybe trying to mirror some WoD/Vampire mechanics and themes?<br /> <br /> I'm really liking the Abyssal elements of death and bleakness in their charms and powers, but man I'm looking forward to seeing how they are done in EX3, hopefully with a design that incorporates more shades of grey and support for mixed games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1522-turkeygiant","name":"turkeygiant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1522_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"999"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-21T18:21:27-08:00","id":318604,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>turkeygiant</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/318040-making-an-abyssal-for-the-first-time?p=318602#post318602\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The other thing I just ran into is figuring out how to respire essence. I'm playing a mortal who is going to pick up an unbound Abyssal Exaltation (No Deathlord or Monstrance) so I can't rely on going back to a shadowland every night, and vampire murder-hobo sprees can be hard to explain to the party. From what I understand a hearthstone is the solution, so I picked one up. It seems like the Abyssal respiration rules are really punitive in a basically un-fun way, were they maybe trying to mirror some WoD/Vampire mechanics and themes?<br /> <br /> I'm really liking the Abyssal elements of death and bleakness in their charms and powers, but man I'm looking forward to seeing how they are done in EX3, hopefully with a design that incorporates more shades of grey and support for mixed games.</div> </div> </div> </div>Remembering the Abyssal spoiler from the Kickstarter i'd say you're gonna expect exactly fifty shades of gray in that book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amateur drawsmith","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2847-thatsmellygoblin","name":"ThatSmellyGoblin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2847_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"188"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-21T18:22:22-08:00","id":318605,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>turkeygiant</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/318040-making-an-abyssal-for-the-first-time?p=318602#post318602\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The other thing I just ran into is figuring out how to respire essence. I'm playing a mortal who is going to pick up an unbound Abyssal Exaltation (No Deathlord or Monstrance) so I can't rely on going back to a shadowland every night, and vampire murder-hobo sprees can be hard to explain to the party. From what I understand a hearthstone is the solution, so I picked one up.</div> </div> </div> </div>See if you can't convince your ST to give you at least half regular mote regen.<br /> <br /> Seriously, Abyssal essence respiration <i>sucks</i>.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://s3.amazonaws.com/ksr/avatars/3507685/Exalted_Back.small.jpg?1370109312\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <hr />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/446-nervaqus987","name":"Nervaqus987","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar446_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-21T18:44:56-08:00","id":318625,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>turkeygiant</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/318040-making-an-abyssal-for-the-first-time?p=318602#post318602\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It seems like the Abyssal respiration rules are really punitive in a basically un-fun way</div> </div> </div> </div>I would say there are a lot more Abyssal mechanics that are punitive and un-fun than just the respiration rules. IIRC, try to dress gothic/funereal, that should help as well. Hearthstone is a good thing too and, yeah, be prepared to use magic to convince people they like to have their blood drank.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>turkeygiant</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/318040-making-an-abyssal-for-the-first-time?p=318602#post318602\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">were they maybe trying to mirror some WoD/Vampire mechanics and themes?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really. The Camarilla is more like the Realm (decaying power structure full of haughty nobles clinging to the trappings of power however they can); the Sabbat is basically a group of cannibalistic soccer hooligans with a religious twist.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-21T18:47:02-08:00","id":318626,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ThatSmellyGoblin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/318040-making-an-abyssal-for-the-first-time?p=318604#post318604\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Remembering the Abyssal spoiler from the Kickstarter i'd say you're gonna expect exactly fifty shades of gray in that book.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I disagree.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/393-godjaw","name":"Godjaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar393_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"665"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-21T19:26:43-08:00","id":318638,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/318040-making-an-abyssal-for-the-first-time?p=318625#post318625\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would say there are a lot more Abyssal mechanics that are punitive and un-fun than just the respiration rules.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wonder why Abyssal mechanics are so weird, I mean, they are hailed as the world-destroying weapon, but they can't regen mote in Creation, sunlight gives them penalty, they have the Spectral keyword, and being CoD make they vulnerable to Holy effects which everyone and their mother has in their arsenal. It's kinda like those aliens from Signs who melt like jelly when they meet water but decide to conquer Earth of all place......<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-21T21:16:26-08:00","id":318668,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ThatSmellyGoblin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/318040-making-an-abyssal-for-the-first-time?p=318604#post318604\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Remembering the Abyssal spoiler from the Kickstarter i'd say you're gonna expect exactly fifty shades of gray in that book.</div> </div> </div> </div>I saw this joke coming as soon as I wrote those words...and steered right into it for the forums enjoyment. Pretty selfless right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1522-turkeygiant","name":"turkeygiant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1522_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"999"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-21T21:20:54-08:00","id":318670,"title":"","content":"Abyssal have to be careful. You don't restore motes normally so you need to socket a hearth stone in Soul Steel. Resonance can be a bitch...in my game with my Abyssal we had a mortal join us...so I had to develop a way to channel it safely. I came up with a charm that let me channel the blight effect of a resonance erruption INTO the body my target. My ST had me develop it. I still get hit with the Stigmata effect, but that isn't so bad.<br /> <br /> The mote regen is a bitch but...talk to your ST, the charm Ravening Mouth can be restored back to normal and that would solve a lot of problems.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-21T21:26:53-08:00","id":318674,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/318040-making-an-abyssal-for-the-first-time?p=318638#post318638\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I wonder why Abyssal mechanics are so weird, I mean, they are hailed as the world-destroying weapon, but they can't regen mote in Creation, sunlight gives them penalty, they have the Spectral keyword, and being CoD make they vulnerable to Holy effects which everyone and their mother has in their arsenal. It's kinda like those aliens from Signs who melt like jelly when they meet water but decide to conquer Earth of all place......<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think the thing is a lot of those weakness can be mitigated in a straight Abyssals game where you are utilising the support of your Deathlord and a entire party of like minded monsters to back you up. Try to join a party of characters from other splats though and they are going to want to travel in the daylight because it is safer, avoid shadowlands because who wants to deal with that, and be armed to the teeth with Holy charms because creatures of darkness are a formidable selection of opponents. Basically all the things that give the Abyssals their potency are also the things that most threaten other splats, and because of that the other splats equip themselves to fight those strengths.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1522-turkeygiant","name":"turkeygiant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1522_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"999"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-21T22:19:13-08:00","id":318697,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>turkeygiant</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/318040-making-an-abyssal-for-the-first-time?p=318674#post318674\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the thing is a lot of those weakness can be mitigated in a straight Abyssals game where you are utilising the support of your Deathlord and a entire party of like minded monsters to back you up.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is a big pain since historically the 3 most prevalent game types are (1) all Solar; (2) all DB; (3) mixed splat. And really, 2e's &quot;you're a Deathlord's bitch or else you're <i>clearly</i> trying to turn back into a Solar&quot; Abyssal methodology wasn't fun either.<br /> <br /> 2e did not do a good job with really building mechanics around the conceit of mixed-splat games til Alchemicals came out. I hope 3e approaches it differently since there's no reason for the authors not to know how often this comes up.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/318040-making-an-abyssal-for-the-first-time?p=318638#post318638\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder why Abyssal mechanics are so weird, I mean, they are hailed as the world-destroying weapon, but they can't regen mote in Creation, sunlight gives them penalty, they have the Spectral keyword, and being CoD make they vulnerable to Holy effects which everyone and their mother has in their arsenal. It's kinda like those aliens from Signs who melt like jelly when they meet water but decide to conquer Earth of all place......</div> </div> </div> </div>The only reasonable explanation is poor 1e game design carried forward.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-22T00:16:39-08:00","id":318782,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/318040-making-an-abyssal-for-the-first-time?p=318638#post318638\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder why Abyssal mechanics are so weird, I mean, they are hailed as the world-destroying weapon, but they can't regen mote in Creation, sunlight gives them penalty, they have the Spectral keyword, and being CoD make they vulnerable to Holy effects which everyone and their mother has in their arsenal. It's kinda like those aliens from Signs who melt like jelly when they meet water but decide to conquer Earth of all place......</div> </div> </div> </div>The basic idea is that Abyssals were designed more as antagonists. In order to use their full power they have to poison the world and spread shadowlands. This was the purpose of the Spectral keyword. Abyssal charms tended to be less expensive than Solar ones, but in exchange, they cost more when used outside of the Underworld. So, when confronted in Creation, an Abyssal will find himself at a disadvantage, so he will try to move back into the local Shadowland, forcing the protagonists to follow him, where he will then find himself at an advantage over them.<br /> <br /> Which is awesome if you tend to use Abyssals as antagonists, but it really sucks if you use them in a mixed party wandering around Creation, because then your Abyssal will almost always find himself at a disadvantage.<br /> <br /> It also didn't help that, even though Abyssals were based around spreading Shadowlands to the point that they had clear mechanical incentives to do so, we never got actual rules on how Shadowlands can be created or spread.<br /> <br /> Regardless though, as the Spectral keyword was errata'd into oblivion, and we saw new optional rules for replacing Resonance, it's clear that the current writers plan to take Abyssals in a very new direction come 3rd edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-22T00:38:41-08:00","id":318784,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/318040-making-an-abyssal-for-the-first-time?p=318782#post318782\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Regardless though, as the Spectral keyword was errata'd into oblivion, and we saw new optional rules for replacing Resonance, it's clear that the current writers plan to take Abyssals in a very new direction come 3rd edition.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is one of the things i'm most looking forward to when it comes to EX3, not getting pigeon-holed by the splat you choose. For me they best way to handle big bad patrons and default character themes in a splat is to provide background and setting material to make those theme appealing to players. <b>DO NOT</b> break their kneecaps with punitive mechanics if they choose to design a character who is unique and stretches or even busts clear through what is considered standard.<br /> <br /> I'm having to work way to hard to prevent this character from extinguishing all life around him by accident, and even more frustrating is making sure he doesn't get a metaphysical sun-burn, or run out of the raw essence that is the most basic and ubiquitous resource in the game for anybody else...<br /> <br /> I think the biggest aw crap moment was when I saw that Ravening Mouth of Melee had been nerfed in the errata, I knew it was OP right away...and I was ok with that lol","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1522-turkeygiant","name":"turkeygiant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1522_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"999"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-22T04:50:53-08:00","id":318853,"title":"","content":"I view Soulsteel Reaper Spirit and Sunlight Bleeding Away as the spiritual successors to Ravening Mouth of (Ability) unfortunately the former is pretty useless on its own due to not creating an Overdrive pool of its own and the latter is essence 4 and they're both Integrity charms.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>success is the ability to go from one failure to the next without any loss of enthusiasm","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1115-the-hug-ninja","name":"The Hug Ninja","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1115_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"324"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-22T12:08:30-08:00","id":319142,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>turkeygiant</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/318040-making-an-abyssal-for-the-first-time?p=318784#post318784\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-ri